Source: this comes entirely from your saved notes, not general knowledge.","references":{"coverage":"sufficient","general_knowledge":false,"explanation":"Entry 31 directly states the SIP amount and cadence: 5,000/month into the index fund on the 3rd, plus the emergency fund target of 6 months of expenses. No other note relates to finance. No general knowledge was needed; the answer is fully supported by the saved note. The global preference for short bullets applies to study help questions, which this is not, so a brief prose answer is used.","live_web":false,"notes":[{"id":31,"content":"Finance: SIP of 5000/month into the index fund on the 3rd. Emergency fund target is 6 months of expenses.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790174140.5062613,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":true},{"id":26,"content":"Quote: 'The purpose of a system is what it does.' - Stafford Beer. Good counter to design intentions.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790174014.8878171,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":3,"content":"Java: ArrayList vs LinkedList. ArrayList gives O(1) random access because it is backed by an array; LinkedList is O(n) for get(i) but O(1) insert/remove at the ends. For my DSA exam I keep mixing these two up.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173527.547001,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":19,"content":"Question I need to answer: why does a Python default argument get evaluated once? Because def is executed once; the default object is shared across calls.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790174014.712186,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":27,"content":"Bug I saw: in DeepNotes, if two structure reviews queue at once, one gets superseded. That is by design (coalescing).","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790174140.3680928,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":29,"content":"Idea dump: spaced repetition on top of the note interpretations. Each concept could become a flashcard. Risk: concepts are too broad.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790174140.4402335,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":12,"content":"SQLite FTS5 note: bm25() returns lower is better; you must ORDER BY rank, not by bm25 ascending. External content tables need triggers to stay in sync.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173748.5360835,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":5,"content":"Prof said today that inheritance is not for code reuse but for substitutability. If B is-a A then anywhere A works, B must work (Liskov). I want to re-read the LSP chapter.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173527.6071672,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":2,"content":"This website will be made into an extension later, for this application. The system will be tracking all kinds of data of the user by default, we can use those contexts to better organize the info.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790171846.66571,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":16,"content":"Personal: I slept badly, 4 hours. Feeling foggy. Need to stop caffeine after 4pm.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173748.6646752,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":3,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":18,"content":"Lecture: the professor's project idea is to build a DBMS for personal notes. It should support semantic retrieval, not just keyword search. Team of 2.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173748.7025278,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":4,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false},{"id":14,"content":"Recipe: Dal tadka - boil toor dal with turmeric, then temper cumin, garlic, dried red chilli, and curry leaves in ghee. Finish with lemon.","source_url":"","source_title":"","created_at":1790173748.625514,"session_id":"dab611ee-abe8-4b3c-987a-f749aa9eb9ac","revision":4,"excerpt_offset":0,"excerpted":false,"cited":false}]},"status":"completed"}
